  "_comment": "GitHub App webhook deliveries for tests/test_github_webhook.py, with synthetic ids, logins and URLs. Headers and payload keys were checked against a real github_app_authorization delivery in the App's Recent Deliveries on 2026-11-20 (GitHub lists it as github_app_authorization.revoked; top-level keys are exactly action and sender; sender.id is a number; no installation). GitHub also sends the legacy SHA-1 X-Hub-Signature, which the handler must never accept in place of X-Hub-Signature-256. Signatures are computed by the tests with a test secret. The signature vector is GitHub's own published example (validating-webhook-deliveries).",
